The South Carolina Heritage Corridor: Discovery Route (SC Discovery Route) is a highway that is part of the South Carolina Heritage Corridor, which contains one other highway, known as the South Carolina Heritage Corridor: Nature Route or the Savannah River Scenic Byway.. The Discovery Route runs for , serving historical sites in cities such as Greenwood, Ninety Six, Anderson, Charleston, Walhalla, Abbeville, Due West, etc. Some sites it also passes by are the Ninety Six National Historic Site, the Edgefield Courthouse, Erskine College, etc.
Route description
The route travels throughout the state generally in a northwest–southeast direction (no signage indicating direction within this route). In the upstate area, it is mostly concurrent with US 178 from Main Street in Anderson to SC 184 in Donalds and from SC 248 near to Epworth Camp Road near Friendship.
In the midlands region, it follows US 25 and US 25 Business into Edgefield. It then enters Aiken via SC 19. After splitting from SC 19, it joins US 78 for quite a while.
Entering the lowcountry, it and US 78 meet US 321, US 301, US 601, US 21, I-95, US 15, and US 178 (once again). The Discovery Route finally splits from US 78 to join SC 27 briefly in Ridgeville. It then joins SC 61 for the rest of its journey. The route meets US 17/SC Nature Route and finally ends at SC 30 shortly afterwards in Charleston.
